# Density tower: what the meter proves, and what mixing removes
register lv2

add v1 water 100mL
measure v1 density

new cylinder
add v2 water 100mL
add v2 table_sugar 50g
measure v2 density

new cylinder
add v3 white_vinegar_5_percent 100mL
measure v3 density

# Each source liquid has a computed density. Putting mutually miscible
# liquids in one cylinder uses the ordinary add operation and therefore
# mixes them; without a slow-pour operation and vertical diffusion state,
# a persistent layered tower would be a false visual claim.
decant v3 v2 0.25
measure v2 density
